From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] system_api: VM type NICKEL_HOST for apps on the device itself

NickelOS's Linux apps run on the device itself, not in a VM. nickel-appd
registers them with Chrome's GuestOS registry as their own type,
NICKEL_HOST, instead of posing as a Crostini VM (docs/host-apps.md). Chrome
carries the same value in its copy of system_api (Chrome patch 0012).

The value is high, so a type ChromiumOS adds later does not take it.

---
diff -ruN a/system_api/dbus/vm_applications/apps.proto b/system_api/dbus/vm_applications/apps.proto
--- a/system_api/dbus/vm_applications/apps.proto
+++ b/system_api/dbus/vm_applications/apps.proto
@@ -77,6 +77,9 @@
   UNKNOWN = 4;
   ARCVM = 5;
   BAGUETTE = 6;
+  // NickelOS: Linux apps on the device itself, no VM. A high value, so a
+  // type ChromiumOS adds later does not take it.
+  NICKEL_HOST = 100;
 }
 // LINT.ThenChange(/vm_tools/concierge/vm_util.cc,../vm_concierge/concierge_service.proto)
 
